.TH OBTURA 1 "November 2026" "Obtura 0.9.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
obtura \- take, annotate and redact screenshots, and record the screen
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B obtura
[\fIOPTION\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Obtura
is a screenshot and screen recording tool for the GNOME desktop. Without an option it
opens its start window. With an option it starts a capture at once, which makes it easy to
bind to a key: when Obtura is already running, the options go to the running Obtura, so
the capture starts without delay.
.PP
After a capture the picture is on the clipboard and Obtura's editor opens: arrows, curves
through several bends, shapes, pen, highlighter, text and callouts, numbered steps, emoji
and symbols, magnifier, spotlight, measure, blur, pixelate, box, Smart Redact (text and QR
codes), crop, cut out, Beautify (backgrounds, pictures, devices), rotate, resize and
combine. Every mark stays editable (and can be turned) until the picture is saved. Blur,
pixelate and box destroy the hidden pixels in the saved file.
.PP
The user guide opens with \fBF1\fR in any Obtura window.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Capture
.TP
.B \-\-region
Select a part of the screen, then open it in the editor.
.TP
.B \-\-screen
Capture the whole screen.
.TP
.B \-\-last\-region
Capture the region chosen last time, without asking (asks when there is none).
.TP
.B \-\-window
Capture a window: GNOME lists the open windows and asks which one (with
\fB\-\-record\fR: record that window).
.TP
.B \-\-scroll
Scrolling capture: select the part of the screen that scrolls, press Enter, then scroll
it slowly with the mouse wheel; Obtura joins what comes into view. Run
\fBobtura \-\-scroll\fR again (or use Obtura's icon in the top bar, or open Obtura) to
finish. Goes with \fB\-\-copy\fR, \fB\-\-save\fR, \fB\-\-ocr\fR, \fB\-\-qr\fR and
\fB\-\-pin\fR like \fB\-\-region\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-delay " N"
Wait \fIN\fR seconds (0 to 30) before capturing; the seconds left show beside Obtura's
icon in the top bar.
.TP
.B \-\-copy
Copy the picture to the clipboard without opening the editor. Obtura then keeps running
in the background, which keeps the clipboard; in a script, start it with \fB&\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-save " [\fIPATH\fR]"
Save the picture as a PNG file without opening the editor. Without \fIPATH\fR it goes to
the save folder (Preferences), named by the file name template. Obtura exits when done.
.TP
.B \-\-ocr
Read the text in the picture, copy it to the clipboard and print it. A region unless
\fB\-\-screen\fR or \fB\-\-last\-region\fR is given. Needs \fBtesseract\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-qr
Read the QR codes in the picture, copy what they hold to the clipboard and print it, one
code per line. A region unless \fB\-\-screen\fR or \fB\-\-last\-region\fR is given.
.TP
.B \-\-pin
Pin the picture on the screen in a small window of its own.
.TP
.BR \-\-pick\-color ", " \-\-pick\-colour
Click anywhere on the screen: the colour is copied and printed as \fB#rrggbb\fR (or as
\fBrgb()\fR or \fBhsl()\fR, as set in Preferences).
.TP
.B \-\-measure
Measure on the screen: drag across something; Enter copies and prints the measurement
(width \(mu height, length and angle, in pixels).
.SS Record
.TP
.B \-\-record
Record an area of the screen (with \fB\-\-screen\fR: a whole screen; with
\fB\-\-window\fR: a window picked in GNOME's list; with \fB\-\-all\-screens\fR: every
shared screen side by side in one video) as set in the Record window: format (MP4, WebM or
GIF), sound, pointer and countdown. Run
\fBobtura \-\-record\fR again to stop; the first command then prints the file saved.
While recording, Obtura's icon in the top bar pauses, resumes and stops.
.SS Other
.TP
.B \-\-library
Open the library of past screenshots.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print the options and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Done.
.TP
.B 1
Failed (or, with \fB\-\-ocr\fR or \fB\-\-qr\fR, nothing found).
.TP
.B 2
Wrong options.
.TP
.B 3
Cancelled (Escape in the region overlay, or the screen sharing was refused).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B obtura \-\-region
The usual keyboard shortcut: choose a region, then annotate it.
.TP
.B obtura \-\-screen \-\-delay 5 \-\-save ~/Pictures/menu.png
Five seconds to open a menu, then the whole screen saved to a file.
.TP
.B obtura \-\-ocr
Copy the text of a part of the screen, for example of a picture or a video.
.TP
.B obtura \-\-scroll \-\-save ~/Pictures/page.png
A whole web page in one picture: select it, scroll it, then run \fBobtura \-\-scroll\fR
again.
.SH KEYBOARD SHORTCUTS
Obtura's own keys (Ctrl+Shift+R and the others) work while an Obtura window is in front.
For keys that work in every app, turn on Preferences \(fc Keys in every app: Obtura adds
Super+Shift+S (capture a region), Super+Shift+T (copy the text of a region) and
Super+Shift+R (start or stop recording) to GNOME's custom shortcuts, unless something else
uses the key. GNOME lets each user bind a key to any other command: Settings \(fc Keyboard
\(fc View and Customize Shortcuts \(fc Custom Shortcuts. Obtura's Preferences list the
commands, with a button to copy each one.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/obtura/settings.json
Preferences, tool styles, the Record window's choices.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/obtura/library/
The library: every capture as it was taken (before any blur), its text, its tags, and the
marks of the last save. Preferences can turn it off or remove old captures.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/obtura/backgrounds/
Pictures chosen as a Beautify background (a copy each).
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/obtura/
The last region chosen, the screens GNOME lets Obtura see (screen sharing), and
.IR obtura.log ,
the log of errors, warnings and crashes (about 1 MB at most; never pictures or their text; it stays on this computer).
.TP
.I ~/.cache/obtura/
The parts of a recording or a scrolling capture under way; removed when it ends.
.TP
.I ~/Pictures/Screenshots/ \fRand\fP ~/Videos/Screencasts/
Where pictures and recordings are saved unless Preferences say otherwise.
.SH PROGRAMS USED WHEN PRESENT
.TP
.B gst\-launch\-1.0
(package gstreamer1.0-tools, with gstreamer1.0-pipewire and the GStreamer plugins) for
recording, joining paused parts and trimming.
.TP
.B tesseract
(packages tesseract-ocr and tesseract-ocr-\fIlanguage\fR) for Copy Text, Smart Redact and
the library search. QR codes are read by Obtura itself.
.SH PRIVACY
Obtura works entirely on this computer. It does not connect to the internet and sends no
data anywhere.
.SH BUGS
